1
00:00:01,819 --> 00:00:02,909
Chapter 13.

2
00:00:04,369 --> 00:00:09,549
Mr. Rochester, it seems, by the surgeon's orders, went to bed early that night,

3
00:00:10,189 --> 00:00:12,270
nor did he rise soon next morning.

4
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:16,610
When he did come down, he was to attend to business.

5
00:00:17,369 --> 00:00:22,009
His agent and some of his tenants were arrived, and waiting to speak with him.

6
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:25,389
Adele and I had now to vacate the library.

7
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:30,349
It would be in daily requisition as a reception room for callers.

8
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:36,529
A fire was lit in an apartment upstairs, and there I carried our books,

9
00:00:37,169 --> 00:00:39,569
and arranged it for the future school room.

10
00:00:41,014 --> 00:00:46,630
I discerned in the course of the morning that Thornfield Hall was a changed place.

11
00:00:47,610 --> 00:00:52,790
No longer silent as a church, it echoed every hour or two to a knock at the door,

12
00:00:53,389 --> 00:00:54,490
or a clang of the bell.

13
00:00:55,330 --> 00:01:01,591
Steps, too, often traversed the hall, and new voices spoke in different keys below.

14
00:01:02,619 --> 00:01:05,290
A rill from the outer world was flowing through it.

15
00:01:05,909 --> 00:01:06,909
It had a master.

16
00:01:08,069 --> 00:01:10,169
For my part, I liked it better.

17
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:14,130
Adele was not easy to teach that day.

18
00:01:14,869 --> 00:01:15,869
She could not apply.

19
00:01:16,689 --> 00:01:19,217
She kept running to the door and looking over the bannisters

20
00:01:19,218 --> 00:01:21,849
to see if she could get a glimpse of Mr. Rochester.

21
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:28,709
Then she coined pretexts to go downstairs, in order, as I shrewdly suspected,

22
00:01:29,290 --> 00:01:32,869
to visit the library, where I knew she was not wanted.

23
00:01:34,029 --> 00:01:40,369
Then, when I got a little angry and made her sit still, she continued to talk

24
00:01:40,370 --> 00:01:46,169
incessantly of her army Monsieur Edouard Fairfax de Rochester, as she dubbed him.

25
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,830
I had not before heard his print more.

26
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:52,549
And to conjecture what presence he had brought her.

27
00:01:53,419 --> 00:01:58,330
For it appears he had intimated the night before, that when his luggage came from

28
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:01,989
milk -coat, there would be found amongst it a

29
00:02:01,990 --> 00:02:05,911
little box in whose contents she had an interest.

30
00:02:07,009 --> 00:02:09,830
Edsela do its signifier said she,

31
00:02:31,479 --> 00:02:37,849
I and my pupil, dined as usual in Mrs. Fairfax's parlour, the afternoon was wild

32
00:02:37,850 --> 00:02:40,590
and snowy, and we passed it in the schoolroom.

33
00:02:41,669 --> 00:02:46,770
At dark, I allowed Edel to put away books and work, and to run downstairs,

34
00:02:47,659 --> 00:02:53,330
for, from the comparative silence below, and from the cessation of appeals to the

35
00:02:53,330 --> 00:02:58,110
doorbell, I conjectured that Mr. Rochester was now at liberty.

36
00:02:59,159 --> 00:03:03,990
Left alone, I walked to the window, but nothing was to be seen thence.

37
00:03:04,819 --> 00:03:07,366
Twilight and Snowflakes together thickened

38
00:03:07,367 --> 00:03:11,190
the air and hid the very shrubs on the lawn.

39
00:03:11,939 --> 00:03:14,750
I let down the curtain and went back to the fireside.

40
00:03:15,764 --> 00:03:18,369
In the clear embers, I was tracing a view.

41
00:03:19,310 --> 00:03:23,169
Not unlike a picture I remembered to have seen of the castle of Heidelberg,

42
00:03:23,869 --> 00:03:30,729
on the Rhine, when Mrs. Fairfax came in, breaking up by her entrance, the fiery

43
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:36,369
mosaic I had been piercing together, and scattering to some heavy unwelcome

44
00:03:36,370 --> 00:03:39,970
thoughts that were beginning to throng on my solitude.

45
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:45,849
Mr. Rochester would be glad if you and your pupil would take tea with him in the

46
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:50,997
drawing -room this evening, said she, he has been so much

47
00:03:50,998 --> 00:03:54,349
engaged all day that he could not ask to see you before.

48
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:58,189
When is his tea time, I inquired?

49
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:02,790
Oh, at six o'clock, he keeps early hours in the country.

50
00:04:03,669 --> 00:04:07,409
You had better change your frock now, I will go with you and fasten it.

51
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:08,970
Here is a candle.

52
00:04:10,404 --> 00:04:12,209
Is it necessary to change my frock?

53
00:04:13,439 --> 00:04:14,549
Yes, you had better.

54
00:04:15,319 --> 00:04:17,790
I always dress for the evening when Mr. Rochester is here.

55
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:21,889
This additional ceremony seemed somewhat stately.

56
00:04:22,729 --> 00:04:27,688
However, I repaired to my room, and, with Mrs. Fairfax's

57
00:04:27,689 --> 00:04:30,849
aid, replaced my blackstuff dress by one of black silk.

58
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:36,130
The best and the only additional one I had, except one of light gray,

59
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:41,790
which, in my low-wood notions of the toilet, I thought to find to be worn,

60
00:04:42,150 --> 00:04:44,069
except on first-rate occasions.

61
00:04:45,419 --> 00:04:47,770
You want a brooch, said Mrs. Fairfax.

62
00:04:48,819 --> 00:04:54,350
I had a single little pearl ornament, which Mrs. Temple gave me as a parting keepsake.

63
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:57,169
I put it on, and then we went downstairs.

64
00:04:58,950 --> 00:05:02,679
Unused as I was to strangers, it was rather a trial, to

65
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:06,349
appear thus formally summoned in Mr. Rochester's presence.

66
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:12,909
I let Mrs. Fairfax proceed me into the dining-room, and kept in her shade as we

67
00:05:12,911 --> 00:05:18,569
crossed that apartment, and, passing the arch, whose curtain was now dropped,

68
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:21,590
entered the elegant recess beyond.

69
00:05:23,169 --> 00:05:27,369
Two axe candles stood lighted on the table, and two on the mantelpiece,

70
00:05:28,209 --> 00:05:32,470
basking in the light and heat of a superb fire, lay pilot.

71
00:05:33,770 --> 00:05:34,950
A del knelt near him.

72
00:05:36,049 --> 00:05:42,170
Half reclined on a couch, appeared Mr. Rochester, his foot supported by the cushion.

73
00:05:42,659 --> 00:05:47,229
He was looking at a del and the the fire shone full on his face.

74
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:51,610
I knew my traveler with his broad and jetty eyebrows.

75
00:05:52,509 --> 00:05:57,130
His square forehead made square by the horizontal sweep of his black hair.

76
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:03,130
I recognized his decisive nose, more remarkable for character than beauty.

77
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:07,869
His full nostrils, denoting, I thought, caller.

78
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:13,889
His grim mouth, chin and jaw, yes, all three were very grim and no mistake.

79
00:06:14,939 --> 00:06:18,222
His shape, now divested of cloak, I perceived

80
00:06:18,223 --> 00:06:21,290
harmonized in squareness with his physiognomy.

81
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:27,830
I suppose it was a good figure in the athletic sense of the term, broad chested

82
00:06:28,229 --> 00:06:31,849
and thin flanked, though neither tall nor graceful.

83
00:06:33,584 --> 00:06:38,509
Mr. Rochester must have been aware of the entrance of Mrs. Fairfax and myself,

84
00:06:39,549 --> 00:06:42,619
but it appeared he was not in the mood to notice

85
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:45,911
us, for he never lifted his head as we approached.

86
00:06:47,319 --> 00:06:51,770
Here is Miss Aia Sir, said Mrs. Fairfax, in her quiet way.

87
00:06:52,759 --> 00:06:57,250
He bowed, still not taking his eyes from the group of the dog and child.

88
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:01,029
Let Miss Aia be seated, said he.

89
00:07:02,110 --> 00:07:05,657
And there was something in the forced stiff bow, in the

90
00:07:05,658 --> 00:07:09,909
impatient yet formal tone, which seemed further to express.

91
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:14,630
What the juice is it to me whether Miss Aia be there or not?

92
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:18,409
At this moment I am not disposed to a cost her.

93
00:07:20,419 --> 00:07:22,689
I sat down quite disembarrassed.

94
00:07:23,779 --> 00:07:27,150
A reception of finished politeness would probably have confused me.

95
00:07:27,939 --> 00:07:32,930
I could not have returned or repaid it by answering grace and elegance on my part.

96
00:07:34,250 --> 00:07:36,909
But harsh caprice laid me under no obligation.

97
00:07:37,849 --> 00:07:44,431
On the contrary, a decent quiescence, under the freak of manner, gave me the advantage.

98
00:07:45,259 --> 00:07:48,849
Besides, the eccentricity of the proceeding was peacant.

99
00:07:49,549 --> 00:07:51,770
I felt interested to see how he would go on.

100
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:54,970
He went on as a statue would.

101
00:07:55,490 --> 00:07:58,270
That is, he neither spoke nor moved.

102
00:07:59,279 --> 00:08:02,529
Mrs. Fairfax seemed to think it necessary that someone should be amiable,

103
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,250
and she began to talk.

104
00:08:05,590 --> 00:08:09,529
Kindly, as usual, and as usual, rather trite.

105
00:08:10,310 --> 00:08:13,369
She can doled with him on the pressure of business he had had all day.

106
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:18,029
On the annoyance it must have been to him with that painful sprain.

107
00:08:19,139 --> 00:08:23,430
Then she commended his patience and perseverance in going through with it.

108
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:27,590
Madam, I should like some tea.

109
00:08:28,470 --> 00:08:30,529
Was the soul rejoinder she got?

110
00:08:31,009 --> 00:08:35,430
She hastened to ring the bell, and when the tray came, she proceeded to

111
00:08:35,431 --> 00:08:39,610
arrange the cups, spoons, etc., with a siguous cellarity.

112
00:08:40,930 --> 00:08:46,169
I and Adele went to the table, but the master did not leave his couch.

113
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:50,150
Will you hand Mr. Rochester's cup?

114
00:08:50,849 --> 00:08:52,270
said Mrs. Fairfax to me.

115
00:08:53,009 --> 00:08:54,810
Adele might perhaps spill it.

116
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:56,790
I did as requested.

117
00:08:57,845 --> 00:09:02,270
As he took the cup from my hand, Adele, thinking the moment propitious for

118
00:09:02,271 --> 00:09:04,830
making a request in my favour, cried out.

119
00:09:06,130 --> 00:09:12,729
Next to Parmasya, Quilia Un Kadio Pau, Mademoiselle Airdon Votre Petit Koffre,

120
00:09:14,110 --> 00:09:16,770
who talks of Kadue, said he gruffly.

121
00:09:17,849 --> 00:09:19,509
Did you expect a present, Miss Aire?

122
00:09:20,459 --> 00:09:21,650
Are you fond of presents?

123
00:09:22,630 --> 00:09:27,310
And he searched my face with eyes that I saw were dark, I rate, and piercing.

124
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:30,169
I hardly know, sir.

125
00:09:30,869 --> 00:09:32,610
I have little experience of them.

126
00:09:33,349 --> 00:09:35,549
They are generally thought pleasant things.

127
00:09:36,930 --> 00:09:37,930
Generally thought.

128
00:09:38,490 --> 00:09:39,490
But what do you think?

129
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:45,270
I should be obliged to take time, sir, before I could give you an answer

130
00:09:45,770 --> 00:09:47,130
worthy of your acceptance.

131
00:09:48,110 --> 00:09:51,349
A present has many faces to it, has it not?

132
00:09:52,159 --> 00:09:56,529
And one should consider all before pronouncing an opinion as to its nature.

133
00:09:57,889 --> 00:10:02,130
Miss Aire, you are not so unsophisticated as Adele.

134
00:10:02,729 --> 00:10:07,209
She demands Akadau, clamorously, the moment she sees me.

135
00:10:08,130 --> 00:10:09,290
You beat about the bush.

136
00:10:10,544 --> 00:10:15,490
Because I have less confidence in my desserts than Adele has, she can prefer

137
00:10:15,491 --> 00:10:19,529
the claim of older acquaintance and the right two of custom.

138
00:10:20,349 --> 00:10:24,250
For she says you have always been in the habit of giving her playthings.

139
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:30,009
But if I had to make out a case, I should be puzzled since I am a stranger

140
00:10:30,759 --> 00:10:33,349
and have done nothing to entitle me to an acknowledgement.

141
00:10:35,169 --> 00:10:37,790
Oh, don't fall back on over modesty.

142
00:10:38,569 --> 00:10:42,509
I have examined Adele and find you have taken great pains with her.

143
00:10:43,150 --> 00:10:46,201
She is not bright, she has no talents, yet in

144
00:10:46,202 --> 00:10:49,330
a short time she has made much improvement.

145
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:52,950
Sir, you have now given me my Kadau.

146
00:10:53,799 --> 00:10:54,990
I am obliged to you.

147
00:10:55,610 --> 00:10:59,209
It is the mead teacher's most covet praise of their pupils' progress.

148
00:11:00,569 --> 00:11:05,009
Humph, said Mr. Rochester, and he took his tea in silence.

149
00:11:06,904 --> 00:11:09,090
Come to the fire, said the master.

150
00:11:09,770 --> 00:11:12,350
When the tray was taken away, and Mrs. Fairfax

151
00:11:12,351 --> 00:11:15,550
had settled into a corner with her knitting.

152
00:11:15,930 --> 00:11:20,770
While Adele was leading me by the hand round the room, showing me the beautiful

153
00:11:20,771 --> 00:11:26,669
books and ornaments on the consoles and chiffoniers, we obeyed as in duty-bound.

154
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,579
Adele wanted to take a seat on my knee, but

155
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:32,710
she was ordered to amuse herself with pilot.

156
00:11:33,669 --> 00:11:35,549
You have been resident in my house three months?

157
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:37,470
Yes, sir.

158
00:11:38,310 --> 00:11:42,810
And you came from from Lloyd's school in Shire.

159
00:11:43,990 --> 00:11:45,830
Ah, a charitable concern.

160
00:11:46,669 --> 00:11:47,669
How long were you there?

161
00:11:48,729 --> 00:11:49,729
Eight years?

162
00:11:50,950 --> 00:11:52,110
Eight years.

163
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:55,009
You must be tenacious of life.

164
00:11:55,950 --> 00:12:00,250
I thought half the time in such a place would have done up any constitution.

165
00:12:01,229 --> 00:12:04,509
No wonder you have rather the look of another world.

166
00:12:05,889 --> 00:12:08,779
I marveled where you had got that sort of face.

167
00:12:09,659 --> 00:12:14,080
When you came on me in Haleine last night, I thought unaccountably of fairy tales,

168
00:12:14,805 --> 00:12:18,599
and had half a mind to demand whether you had bewitched my horse.

169
00:12:19,919 --> 00:12:20,919
I'm not sure yet.

170
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,200
Who are your parents?

171
00:12:22,619 --> 00:12:23,619
I have none.

172
00:12:24,790 --> 00:12:26,419
Nor ever had, I suppose.

173
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:28,680
Do you remember them?

174
00:12:28,799 --> 00:12:29,799
No.

175
00:12:37,189 --> 00:12:38,189
I thought for whom, sir?

176
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:42,919
For the men in green, it was a proper moonlight evening for them.

177
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:49,800
Did I break through one of your rings that you spread that damned ice on the causeway?

178
00:12:50,979 --> 00:12:51,979
I shook my head.

179
00:12:53,229 --> 00:12:57,254
The men in green all foresoaked England a hundred

180
00:12:57,255 --> 00:13:00,459
years ago, said I, speaking seriously as he had done.

181
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:06,299
And not even in Haleine, or the fields about it, could you find trace of them?

182
00:13:07,979 --> 00:13:11,103
I don't think either summer or harvest or winter

183
00:13:11,104 --> 00:13:14,100
moon will ever shine on their revels more.

184
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:19,630
Mrs Fairfax had dropped her knitting, and with raised

185
00:13:19,631 --> 00:13:22,700
eyebrows seemed wondering what sort of talk this was.

186
00:13:24,299 --> 00:13:26,319
Well, resumed, Mr. Rochester.

187
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:31,279
If you disown parents, you must have some sort of dancefolk, uncles and aunts.

188
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:33,819
No, none that I ever saw.

189
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:35,680
And you're home?

190
00:13:36,139 --> 00:13:37,139
I have none.

191
00:13:38,119 --> 00:13:40,040
Where do your brothers and sisters live?

192
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:42,740
I have no brothers or sisters.

193
00:13:43,639 --> 00:13:45,400
Who recommended you to come here?

194
00:13:46,369 --> 00:13:50,840
I advertised, and Mrs. Fairfax answered my advertisement.

195
00:13:52,150 --> 00:13:56,799
Yes, said the good lady, who now knew what ground we were upon.

196
00:13:57,759 --> 00:14:01,220
And I am daily thankful for the choice providence led me to make.

197
00:14:02,259 --> 00:14:05,039
Miss Aya has been an invaluable companion to

198
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:08,800
me, and a kind and careful teacher to Adele.

199
00:14:09,805 --> 00:14:11,919
Don't trouble yourself to give her a character.

200
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,840
Returned, Mr. Rochester.

201
00:14:14,959 --> 00:14:16,540
Eulogyums will not bias me.

202
00:14:17,389 --> 00:14:18,819
I shall judge for myself.

203
00:14:20,409 --> 00:14:21,919
She began by filling my horse.

204
00:14:22,985 --> 00:14:26,560
Sir, said Mrs. Fairfax, I have to thank her for this sprain.

205
00:14:27,459 --> 00:14:28,580
The widow looked bewildered.

206
00:14:29,775 --> 00:14:32,220
Miss Aya, have you ever lived in a town?

207
00:14:33,119 --> 00:14:34,119
No, sir.

208
00:14:34,639 --> 00:14:35,819
Have you seen much society?

209
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:42,319
None but the pupils and teachers of low wood, and now the inmates of Thornfield.

210
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:44,680
Have you read much?

211
00:14:45,639 --> 00:14:51,980
Only such books has came in my way, and they have not been numerous or very learned.

212
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:54,400
You have lived the life of a nun.

213
00:14:55,479 --> 00:14:57,900
No doubt you are well drilled in religious forms.

214
00:14:59,279 --> 00:15:03,779
Brockelhurst, who I understand directs low wood, is a person, is he not?

215
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,240
Yes, sir.

216
00:15:07,169 --> 00:15:10,081
And you girls probably worshipped him, as a convent

217
00:15:10,082 --> 00:15:12,500
full of religiouses would worship their director.

218
00:15:13,290 --> 00:15:14,290
Oh no.

219
00:15:15,150 --> 00:15:16,150
You are very cool.

220
00:15:16,299 --> 00:15:16,479
No.

221
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:18,040
What?

222
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:20,240
A novice not worship her priest?

223
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:21,919
That sounds blasphemous.

224
00:15:23,299 --> 00:15:27,619
I disliked Mr. Brockelhurst, and I was not alone in the feeling.

225
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:29,419
He is a harsh man.

226
00:15:29,979 --> 00:15:33,020
At once pompous and meddling, he cut off our hair.

227
00:15:33,869 --> 00:15:36,654
And for economy's sake bought us bad needles

228
00:15:36,655 --> 00:15:39,780
and thread, with which we could hardly sew.

229
00:15:41,459 --> 00:15:45,489
That was very false economy, remarked Mrs. Fairfax,

230
00:15:45,490 --> 00:15:49,080
who now again caught the drift of the dialogue.

231
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:54,900
And was that the head and front of his offending demanded Mr. Rochester.

232
00:15:55,869 --> 00:15:59,900
He starved us when he had the sole superintendents of the provision

233
00:15:59,901 --> 00:16:03,060
department before the committee was appointed.

234
00:16:03,939 --> 00:16:09,020
And he bored us with long lectures once a week, and with evening readings from books

235
00:16:09,021 --> 00:16:11,947
of his own inditing about sudden deaths and

236
00:16:11,948 --> 00:16:15,741
judgments which made us afraid to go to bed.

237
00:16:17,029 --> 00:16:19,099
What age were you when you went to low wood?

238
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:20,880
About ten.

239
00:16:22,279 --> 00:16:23,919
And you stayed there eight years.

240
00:16:24,599 --> 00:16:26,020
You are now then eighteen.

241
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,240
I ascended.

242
00:16:29,119 --> 00:16:30,759
Arithmetic you see as useful.

243
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:35,659
Without its aid, I should hardly have been able to guess your age.

244
00:16:36,599 --> 00:16:39,612
It is a point difficult to fix where the features and

245
00:16:39,613 --> 00:16:42,419
countenance are so much at variance as in your case.

246
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:45,340
And now what did you learn at low wood?

247
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:46,900
Can you play?

248
00:16:47,419 --> 00:16:48,419
A little.

249
00:16:49,369 --> 00:16:51,880
Of course, that is the established answer.

250
00:16:52,599 --> 00:16:53,599
Go into the library.

251
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:54,700
I mean, if you please.

252
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:57,299
Excuse my tone of command.

253
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:01,060
I am used to say, do this, and it is done.

254
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:05,119
I cannot alter my customary habits for one new inmate.

255
00:17:06,209 --> 00:17:07,720
Go then into the library.

256
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:09,220
Take a candle with you.

257
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:10,380
Leave the door open.

258
00:17:10,639 --> 00:17:12,419
Sit down to the piano and play a tune.

259
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:16,020
I departed, obeying his directions.

260
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:20,580
Enough, he called out in a few minutes.

261
00:17:21,459 --> 00:17:22,619
You play a little, I see.

262
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:28,439
Like any other English schoolgirl, perhaps rather better than some, but not well.

263
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:30,720
I closed the piano and returned.

264
00:17:32,279 --> 00:17:33,680
Mr. Rochester continued.

265
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:39,619
Adele showed me some sketches this morning, which she said were yours.

266
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:43,319
I don't know whether they were entirely of your doing.

267
00:17:43,799 --> 00:17:45,419
Probably a master aided you.

268
00:17:46,395 --> 00:17:48,880
No, indeed, I interjected.

269
00:17:48,979 --> 00:17:50,259
Ah, that prick's pride.

270
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:55,759
Well, fetch me your portfolio if you can vouch for its contents being original.

271
00:17:56,950 --> 00:17:59,040
But don't pass your word unless you are certain.

272
00:17:59,939 --> 00:18:01,439
I can recognize patchwork.

273
00:18:02,805 --> 00:18:06,860
Then I will say nothing, and you shall judge for yourself, sir.

274
00:18:08,229 --> 00:18:09,939
I brought the portfolio from the library.

275
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:17,279
Approach the table, said he, and I wield it to his couch.

276
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:22,459
Adele and Mrs. Fairfax drew near to see the pictures.

277
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:27,380
No crowding, said Mr. Rochester.

278
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:31,283
Take the drawings from my hand as I finish with

279
00:18:31,284 --> 00:18:35,061
them, but don't push your faces up to mine.

280
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:38,840
He deliberately scrutinized each sketch and painting.

281
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,080
Three, he laid aside.

282
00:18:41,939 --> 00:18:45,240
The others, when he had examined them, he swept from him.

283
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:49,741
Take them off to the other table, Mrs. Fairfax, said

284
00:18:49,742 --> 00:18:54,580
he, and look at them with Adele, you, glancing at me.

285
00:18:55,479 --> 00:18:57,880
Resume your seat and answer my questions.

286
00:18:58,860 --> 00:19:01,380
I perceive those pictures were done by one hand.

287
00:19:02,159 --> 00:19:03,159
Was that hand yours?

288
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:05,340
Yes.

289
00:19:06,250 --> 00:19:07,799
And when did you find time to do them?

290
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:11,360
They have taken much time and some thought.

291
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:14,577
I did them in the last two vacations I spent

292
00:19:14,578 --> 00:19:17,361
at Lowwood, when I had no other occupation.

293
00:19:18,290 --> 00:19:19,490
Where did you get your copies?

294
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:21,540
Out of my head.

295
00:19:22,430 --> 00:19:24,180
That head I see now on your shoulders?

296
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Yes, sir.

297
00:19:26,419 --> 00:19:28,259
Has it other furniture of the same kind within?

298
00:19:29,689 --> 00:19:30,799
I should think it may have.

299
00:19:31,479 --> 00:19:32,479
I should hope?

300
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:33,740
Better.

301
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:38,400
He spread the pictures before him, and again surveyed them alternately.

302
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:43,900
While he is so occupied, I will tell you, reader, what they are.

303
00:19:44,569 --> 00:19:49,279
And first, I must premise that they are nothing wonderful.

304
00:19:50,299 --> 00:19:56,159
The subjects had indeed risen vividly on my mind, as I saw them with the spiritual

305
00:19:56,161 --> 00:19:59,431
eye before I attempted to embody them they were

306
00:19:59,432 --> 00:20:03,159
striking, but my hand would not second my fancy.

307
00:20:03,930 --> 00:20:09,920
And in each case, it had wrought out but a pale portrait of the thing I had conceived.

308
00:20:10,619 --> 00:20:12,880
These pictures were in watercolors.

309
00:20:13,779 --> 00:20:19,119
The first represented clouds low and livid, rolling over a swollen sea.

310
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:21,580
All the distance was in eclipse.

311
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:24,200
So too was the foreground.

312
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:28,060
Or rather, the nearest billows for there was no land.

313
00:20:28,930 --> 00:20:34,500
One gleam of light lifted into relief, a half submerged mast, on which sat a

314
00:20:34,501 --> 00:20:38,400
comorant, dark and large, with wings flecked with foam.

315
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:44,340
Its beak held a gold bracelet set with gems, that I had touched with as brilliant

316
00:20:44,341 --> 00:20:47,268
tints as my palette could yield, and as

317
00:20:47,269 --> 00:20:50,201
glittering distinctness as my pencil could impart.

318
00:20:51,479 --> 00:20:57,640
Sinking below the burden mast, a drowned corpse glanced through the green water.

319
00:20:58,290 --> 00:21:01,647
A fair arm was the only limb clearly visible,

320
00:21:01,648 --> 00:21:05,341
once the bracelet had been washed or torn.

321
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:10,360
The second picture contained for foreground only the dim peak of a hill,

322
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,919
with grass and some leaves slanting as if by a breeze.

323
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:20,439
Beyond and above, spread an expanse of sky dark blue as at twilight.

324
00:21:21,459 --> 00:21:24,919
Rising into the sky was a woman's shape to the bust,

325
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:28,139
portrayed in tints as dusk and soft as I could combine.

326
00:21:29,569 --> 00:21:31,939
The dim forehead was crowned with a star.

327
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:36,560
The lineaments below were seen as through the suffusion of vapor.

328
00:21:37,599 --> 00:21:39,580
The eyes shone dark and wild.

329
00:21:40,439 --> 00:21:47,280
The hair streamed shadowy, like a beamless cloud torn by storm or by electric travail.

330
00:21:47,950 --> 00:21:51,599
On the neck lay a pale reflection like moonlight.

331
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:56,087
The same faint lustre touched the train of thin clouds

332
00:21:56,088 --> 00:22:00,080
from which rose and bowed this vision of the evening star.

333
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:05,479
The third showed the pinnacle of an iceberg piercing a polar winter sky,

334
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:12,600
a muster of northern lights reared their dim lances close serried along the horizon.

335
00:22:13,430 --> 00:22:16,939
Throwing these interdistance rows in the foreground.

336
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:18,740
A head.

337
00:22:19,064 --> 00:22:24,220
A colossal head inclined towards the iceberg and resting against it.

338
00:22:24,979 --> 00:22:28,927
Two thin hands joined under the forehead and supporting

339
00:22:28,929 --> 00:22:32,060
it drew up before the lower features a sable veil.

340
00:22:32,939 --> 00:22:37,819
A brow quite bloodless, white as bone and an eye hollow and fixed.

341
00:22:38,470 --> 00:22:42,720
Blank of meaning but for the glassiness of despair alone were visible.

342
00:22:43,849 --> 00:22:50,439
Above the temples amidst wreathed turban folds of black drapery, vague in its

343
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:54,475
character in consistency as cloud gleamed a ring of

344
00:22:54,476 --> 00:22:58,479
white flame, gemmed with sparkles of a more lurid tinge.

345
00:22:59,259 --> 00:23:02,459
This pale crescent was the likeness of a kingly crown.

346
00:23:03,299 --> 00:23:06,740
What it diademed was the shape which shape had none.

347
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:10,560
Were you happy when you painted these pictures?

348
00:23:11,419 --> 00:23:12,880
Asked Mr. Rochester presently.

349
00:23:13,549 --> 00:23:14,959
I was absorbed, sir.

350
00:23:15,459 --> 00:23:16,900
Yes, and I was happy.

351
00:23:17,970 --> 00:23:23,240
To paint them in short was to enjoy one of the keenest pleasures I have ever known.

352
00:23:24,630 --> 00:23:26,000
That is not saying much.

353
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:29,819
Your pleasures, by your own account, have been few.

354
00:23:30,639 --> 00:23:33,616
But I dare say you did exist in a kind of artist's

355
00:23:33,617 --> 00:23:37,459
dreamland while you blent and arranged these strange tints.

356
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:39,819
Did you sit at them long each day?

357
00:23:41,630 --> 00:23:47,020
I had nothing else to do because it was the vacation, and I sat at them from

358
00:23:47,021 --> 00:23:49,439
morning till noon and from noon till night.

359
00:23:50,159 --> 00:23:54,360
The length of the mid-summer days favored my inclination to apply.

360
00:23:56,330 --> 00:24:00,400
And you felt self-satisfied with the result of your ardent labours?

361
00:24:01,099 --> 00:24:02,099
Far from it.

362
00:24:02,764 --> 00:24:07,900
I was tormented by the contrast between my idea and my handywork.

363
00:24:09,375 --> 00:24:15,299
In each case, I had imagined something which I was quite powerless to realise.

364
00:24:16,520 --> 00:24:17,540
Not quite.

365
00:24:18,500 --> 00:24:22,459
You have secured the shadow of your thought, but no more probably.

366
00:24:23,630 --> 00:24:28,259
You had not enough of the artist's skill and science to give it full being,

367
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:32,900
yet the drawings are for a schoolgirl peculiar.

368
00:24:34,290 --> 00:24:36,700
As to the thoughts, they are elfish.

369
00:24:37,439 --> 00:24:40,520
These eyes in the evening star, you must have seen in a dream.

370
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:45,421
How could you make them look so clear, and yet not at

371
00:24:45,422 --> 00:24:49,419
all brilliant, for the planet above quells their rays?

372
00:24:50,494 --> 00:24:52,840
And what meaning is that in their solemn depth?

373
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:55,959
And who taught you to paint wind?

374
00:24:57,180 --> 00:25:02,960
There is a high gale in that sky, and on this hilltop, where did you see Latmos?

375
00:25:03,645 --> 00:25:04,645
For that is Latmos.

376
00:25:05,220 --> 00:25:05,340
There.

377
00:25:06,220 --> 00:25:07,220
Put the drawings away.

378
00:25:08,799 --> 00:25:12,659
I had scarce tied the strings of the portfolio, when looking at his watch,

379
00:25:13,099 --> 00:25:15,740
he said abruptly, it is nine o'clock.

380
00:25:16,540 --> 00:25:19,400
What are you about, Miss Eyre, to let Adele sit up so long?

381
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:21,020
Take her to bed.

382
00:25:22,599 --> 00:25:25,580
Adele went to kiss him before quitting the room.

383
00:25:26,490 --> 00:25:29,880
He endured the caress, but scarcely seemed to relish

384
00:25:29,881 --> 00:25:33,599
it, more than pilot would have done, nor so much.

385
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:40,479
I wish you all good night now, said he, making a movement of the hand

386
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:46,940
towards the door, in token that he was tired of our company and wished to dismiss us.

387
00:25:47,639 --> 00:25:49,479
Mrs Fairfax folded up her knitting.

388
00:25:50,450 --> 00:25:51,450
I took my portfolio.

389
00:25:52,319 --> 00:25:57,619
We curtsied to him, received a frigid bow in return, and so withdrew.

390
00:25:59,150 --> 00:26:05,000
You said Mr. Rochester was not strikingly peculiar, Mrs. Fairfax, I observed,

391
00:26:05,439 --> 00:26:08,880
when I rejoined her in her room, after putting Adele to bed.

392
00:26:10,380 --> 00:26:11,919
Well, is he?

393
00:26:12,840 --> 00:26:13,840
I think so.

394
00:26:14,229 --> 00:26:15,779
He is very changeful and abrupt.

395
00:26:17,310 --> 00:26:20,826
True, no doubt he may appear so to a stranger, but I

396
00:26:20,827 --> 00:26:23,819
am so accustomed to his manner, I never think of it.

397
00:26:24,569 --> 00:26:28,619
And then, if he has peculiarities of temper, allowance should be made.

398
00:26:29,340 --> 00:26:30,340
Why?

399
00:26:30,665 --> 00:26:35,880
Partly because it is his nature, and we can none of us help our nature,

400
00:26:36,750 --> 00:26:39,889
and partly because he has painful thoughts, no

401
00:26:39,890 --> 00:26:43,119
doubt, to harass him and make his spirits unequal.

402
00:26:44,459 --> 00:26:47,840
What about family troubles for one thing?

403
00:26:48,889 --> 00:26:49,919
But he has no family.

404
00:26:50,919 --> 00:26:54,694
Not now, but he has had, or at least relatives,

405
00:26:54,695 --> 00:26:58,201
he lost his elder brother a few years since.

406
00:26:58,919 --> 00:26:59,919
His elder brother?

407
00:27:00,340 --> 00:27:01,340
Yes.

408
00:27:01,639 --> 00:27:05,939
The present Mr. Rochester has not been very long in possession of the property,

409
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:08,119
only about nine years.

410
00:27:09,470 --> 00:27:11,779
Nine years is a tolerable time.

411
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:17,340
Was he so very fond of his brother as to be still inconsolable for his loss?

412
00:27:19,270 --> 00:27:20,799
Why no, perhaps not.

413
00:27:21,819 --> 00:27:25,080
I believe there were some misunderstandings between them.

414
00:27:26,380 --> 00:27:31,319
Mr. Roland Rochester was not quite just to Mr. Edward,

415
00:27:31,320 --> 00:27:34,919
and perhaps he prejudiced his father against him.

416
00:27:36,080 --> 00:27:41,600
The old gentleman was fond of money and anxious to keep the family estate together.

417
00:27:42,229 --> 00:27:48,020
He did not like to diminish the property by division, and yet he was anxious that

418
00:27:48,021 --> 00:27:53,920
Mr. Edward should have wealth, too, to keep up the consequence of the name.

419
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:59,685
And soon after he was of age, some steps were taken that

420
00:27:59,686 --> 00:28:03,740
were not quite fair and made a great deal of mischief.

421
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:10,959
Old Mr. Rochester and Mr. Roland combined to bring Mr. Edward into what he

422
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:15,779
considered a painful position, for the sake of making his fortune.

423
00:28:16,810 --> 00:28:22,580
What the precise nature of that position was I never clearly knew, but his spirit

424
00:28:22,580 --> 00:28:26,380
could not brook what he had to suffer in it.

425
00:28:26,990 --> 00:28:28,380
He is not very forgiving.

426
00:28:29,430 --> 00:28:36,120
He broke with his family, and now for many years he has led an unsettled kind of life.

427
00:28:36,650 --> 00:28:41,220
I don't think he has ever been resident at Thornfield for a fortnight together.

428
00:28:41,900 --> 00:28:45,919
Since the death of his brother without a will left him master of the estate,

429
00:28:46,799 --> 00:28:50,080
and indeed, no wonder he shuns the old place.

430
00:28:51,529 --> 00:28:52,639
Why should he shun it?

431
00:28:53,930 --> 00:28:55,479
Perhaps he thinks it glue me.

432
00:28:56,439 --> 00:28:58,340
The answer was evasive.

433
00:28:59,430 --> 00:29:04,740
I should have liked something clearer, but Mrs. Fairfax either could not or would

434
00:29:04,741 --> 00:29:09,364
not give me more explicit information of the origin and nature of Mr.

435
00:29:09,365 --> 00:29:11,241
Rochester's trials.

436
00:29:12,139 --> 00:29:15,701
She averred they were a mystery to herself, and

437
00:29:15,702 --> 00:29:18,979
that what she knew was chiefly from conjecture.

438
00:29:20,139 --> 00:29:27,061
It was evident indeed that she wished me to drop the subject which I did accordingly.
